From 60955b1bab28261b677e557aa573965445a1ba45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zhixiang Zhao <matthewzhaocc@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 00:39:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] xfrm: state: prefer the CPU's own SA over a newer
 fallback

xfrm_state_look_at() lets a valid state whose pcpu_num matches the
current CPU replace a fallback state as best. The km.dying and
curlft.add_time tie-breakers that follow compare states of both kinds,
though, so a fallback added after the CPU's own state replaces that
state as best.

This happens when a per-CPU SA is installed before the fallback, for
example a CPU SA that the peer initiated and the local key manager
installed as responder. xfrm_state_find() then sees that best is not
this CPU's state and starts a per-CPU acquire for a CPU that already
has a valid SA. The key manager discards that acquire as a duplicate,
and the larval state stays until it expires (165 seconds with
strongSwan). Packets on that CPU are dropped meanwhile, or are carried
on the fallback SA with "xfrm: state: use the fallback SA while a
per-CPU acquire is pending" applied, and the CPU's own SA is never
used.

Apply the dying and age tie-breakers only between states of the same
kind. A state for the current CPU still replaces a fallback, and
states without a CPU ID, which all have pcpu_num UINT_MAX, are chosen
exactly as before.

The problem was found and the fix drafted with AI coding assistants
(OpenAI Codex and Anthropic Claude) while testing per-CPU SAs for a
VXLAN-over-IPsec deployment. The analysis, reproducer and fix were
reviewed by the submitter.

Fixes: 1ddf9916ac09 ("xfrm: Add support for per cpu xfrm state handling.")
---
 net/xfrm/xfrm_state.c | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/xfrm/xfrm_state.c b/net/xfrm/xfrm_state.c
index bfba1abce..ff6cb75c7 100644
--- a/net/xfrm/xfrm_state.c
+++ b/net/xfrm/xfrm_state.c
@@ -1358,9 +1358,10 @@ static void xfrm_state_look_at(struct xfrm_policy *pol, struct xfrm_state *x,
 
 		if (!*best ||
 		    ((*best)->pcpu_num == UINT_MAX && x->pcpu_num == pcpu_id) ||
-		    (*best)->km.dying > x->km.dying ||
-		    ((*best)->km.dying == x->km.dying &&
-		     (*best)->curlft.add_time < x->curlft.add_time))
+		    ((*best)->pcpu_num == x->pcpu_num &&
+		     ((*best)->km.dying > x->km.dying ||
+		      ((*best)->km.dying == x->km.dying &&
+		       (*best)->curlft.add_time < x->curlft.add_time))))
 			*best = x;
 	} else if (x->km.state == XFRM_STATE_ACQ) {
 		if (x->pcpu_num != UINT_MAX && x->pcpu_num != pcpu_id)
